      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why should it be null?? What\u0027s wrong with returning an instance whose method would all through?\n\nGenerally, changing @NonNull method/field to @Nullable can cause subtle issues in the callsites.\n\nFor example, in code like `var zp \u003d ZYGOTE_PROCESS; (alot of code)...; zp.foo()`, when you get an NPE in the last line, it\u0027s unclear until you look into the code why you got an NPE and if that\u0027s actually expected (e.g. there may be `zp \u003d\u003d null` somewhere). But if you get a \"this method is not supported on ravenwood\" exception, it\u0027d be clear.\n\n(If there\u0027s a reason we absolutely don\u0027t want to use a real instance, this may be the first case where we want to remove the field on ravenwood.)",
